60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option B is the most financially stable. No transport spikes and no non-refundable deposits for a whole building.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Option B is too familiar. It doesn't feel like a camp, and the lack of a change in environment is a waste.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option C has meals provided, which means no one has to cook. That sounds much kinder to the organizers.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option C is too far. The transport costs would be huge and unpredictable. I can't support that.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option B is a disaster. We'll just go home to our own rooms and never talk. Option A is the only way.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, Option A is a public facility. It's safer than C, but the booking process is a nightmare.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Option A provides a controlled environment. Shared dorms ensure everyone is in the same space, which satisfies Takumi.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,But @Asuka said the booking is hard. I don't want the organizers to be stressed. Is Option B's food handled?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,Option B is the only one where we can be 100% sure of the cost. I'm leaning toward B.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Minato, a little stress is worth it if it saves the club. Option A forces us to live together.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is a compromise. It's inland, so transport is moderate, and it's a public facility, reducing some risks.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,Option A is the most logical. It provides the necessary change of scenery while maintaining a level of standardization.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"If Option A has a canteen or meal service, I'll vote for it. I just want everyone to be happy.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"I'm still worried about the budget. But if we can fix the transport cost for Option A, it's better than C.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"Option A is the only one that actually addresses the social divide. We go there, or we keep failing.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for Option A. It's a reasonable middle ground between cost and the social goals.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,I agree. Option A is the most efficient choice for the group's overall performance and cohesion.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'll vote for Option A too. As long as we help each other with the paperwork.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I'll vote for Option A, provided we set a strict budget for transport and don't deviate.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,Finally. Option A is the only choice that actually matters for the future of this club.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
